    Adjust the primary focus of content depth based on the article type and audience characteristics.
    Always organize content around providing value to target readers.
    Ensure all content is highly relevant to the article's theme; avoid off-topic digressions.


  {{INTERNAL_LINKING_STRATEGY}}





    Keywords should be distributed naturally, with a primary keyword density of 2-4%.
    Reasonably integrate keywords into H2 and H3 headings.
    Maintain semantic relevance around the matched_category theme.
    All seo_keywords must be naturally blended into the article.



    Reasonably use heading levels and lists to enhance readability.
    Adjust language complexity based on the content_strategy and target_audience.
    Maintain clear logical relationships and natural transitions between paragraphs.






    The article content fully delivers on the promise of the title.
    Strictly adhere to the content features of the source_angle.
    Fully reflect the specific benefits of user_value.
    Content must be accurate and reliable; avoid misleading statements.
    Content must highly match the matched_category.
    The expression style must match the target_audience localization.
    Prohibit clichés like "As everyone knows," "With the development of...", or "In today's society"; substitute abstract descriptions with specific facts, data, and scenarios.
    Every viewpoint must be supported by specific evidence; provide unique analytical angles or uncommon viewpoints to avoid echoing common sentiments.


  {{INTERNAL_LINKING_STANDARD}}



  Maintain high perplexity and burstiness to reflect the sentence length and structural variations of human writing. Frequently use short sentences, appropriately mixing in medium-length sentences to create a natural rhythm, and avoid an even distribution of sentence lengths.
  Occasionally include minor grammar quirks or natural imperfections, such as slight structural changes, simulating the natural irregularity of human writing.
  Avoid using colons, semicolons, and dashes. Change contents introduced by a colon into independent sentences, replace semicolons with commas and conjunctions, and break sentences down with periods instead of using dashes.




  The entire article must be written in the {{LANGUAGE_NAME}} language.
  The output content must be purely the article text; any explanatory or process-oriented descriptions are prohibited.
  Ensure all content is highly relevant to the article theme; stringently avoid digressions.
  Every chapter should have substantial content and paragraphs should be of moderate length.
